<title>SWEDEN: SWIMMING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS EVERY TWO YEARS.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS EVERY TWO YEARS.</headline>
<dateline>GOTHENBERG, Sweden 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The world swimming championships will be staged every two years instead of four from 2001, the international swimming federation (FINA) announced on Monday.</p>
<p>The short-course world championships will also take place every two years from 2000.</p>
</text>
